(Kongdet : Bring Singha here, ASAP!)

268
00:26:51,470 --> 00:26:52,470
Got any Pad Kaprao?

269
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:56,160
You're asking for Kaprao in a hospital?

270
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:58,530
I'll go out and buy it for you.

271
00:26:59,180 --> 00:27:00,090
What kind of Kaprao do you want?

272
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:04,440
Wow, who would ever believe this?

273
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,840
Seven nights in the hospital,
and he wakes up walking like nothing happened.

274
00:27:09,410 --> 00:27:10,720
Hey, wait for me!

275
00:27:11,570 --> 00:27:12,420
- Hey.
- What are you mumbling about?

276
00:27:14,430 --> 00:27:15,510
Look, walking like a pro.

277
00:27:24,780 --> 00:27:26,540
If you'd been here that day,
you probably wouldn't have crashed

278
00:27:28,670 --> 00:27:30,290
That’s got nothing to do with it. Didn’t you see?

279
00:27:30,730 --> 00:27:31,750
There isn't a scratch on me.

280
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:34,450
Yeah, sure. I believe you.

281
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:36,660
And I'm still hungry!

282
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:39,840
I haven't even finished eating and
I'm already getting kicked out of the hospital.

283
00:27:40,450 --> 00:27:42,200
Alright. I'll buy you that Kaprao.

284
00:27:43,190 --> 00:27:44,320
You're such a nag.

285
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:48,600
Hey

286
00:27:48,970 --> 00:27:50,510
I'll be right back. You guys keep talking.

287
00:27:51,610 --> 00:27:52,490
- Where to?
- Why?

288
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:53,600
Hey, check on the shop.

289
00:27:53,790 --> 00:27:54,630
Working.

290
00:27:54,890 --> 00:27:56,570
- Suit yourself, man. Be my guest.
- You bastard!

291
00:27:56,960 --> 00:27:57,730
So busy.

292
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:59,880
Are you going to check on the shop
and customers, or just go and eat with them?

293
00:28:00,190 --> 00:28:01,640
- Damn you!
- You're a real asshole.

294
00:28:01,760 --> 00:28:04,580
Other shops recommend their menu, but this
asshole just says, Get this one, I like it!

295
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:09,650
- So busy, man! The place is packed.
- Busy, my ass! There are only six tables.

296
00:28:11,240 --> 00:28:13,000
- Nah, Joe is just...
- Huh?

297
00:28:13,040 --> 00:28:15,740
The doc was stuttering
when I asked him what happened to Singha.

298
00:28:16,040 --> 00:28:18,720
You should've told him Singh is basically The Hulk.

299
00:28:18,870 --> 00:28:20,390
He’s a superhero, a superhuman.

300
00:28:20,650 --> 00:28:21,660
He’s tough.

301
00:28:21,860 --> 00:28:23,390
Because he's been exposed
to so many chemicals.

302
00:28:24,630 --> 00:28:26,490
Geez, so aggressive!

303
00:28:26,660 --> 00:28:29,160
Watch it! I'll have my crew
from the squid boat come over and kick your ass.

304
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:31,040
- You're such a sadist.
- Yeah, for real.

305
00:28:34,510 --> 00:28:35,980
Squid fishing, you idiot!

306
00:28:36,250 --> 00:28:37,630
What a weird question.

307
00:28:37,670 --> 00:28:38,560
Hey, you guys.

308
00:28:42,050 --> 00:28:43,170
Did you see something over there?

309
00:28:47,980 --> 00:28:48,920
- Where?
- Umm.

310
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:51,920
- There’s nothing there. Not even a single dog.
- Yeah, nothing.

311
00:28:53,780 --> 00:28:55,140
Are you high on IV fluids or something?

312
00:28:55,380 --> 00:28:56,750
Why don't you go to bed? Or just go home?

313
00:28:57,500 --> 00:28:58,850
- You're freaking losing it.
- Yeah.

314
00:28:59,740 --> 00:29:02,800
- Do you have a concussion or something?
- Then forget it. There's nothing there.

315
00:29:03,630 --> 00:29:06,180
- Oh my god.
- He already said that once back at the hospital.

316
00:29:10,130 --> 00:29:11,170
What the hell is with this wind?

317
00:29:13,100 --> 00:29:16,460
What is it this time, Singha?
Why are you rubbing your eyes so hard?

318
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:20,080
- Singha.
- Hey.

319
00:29:20,430 --> 00:29:21,770
Your eyes are super red.

320
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:25,370
- Singha. Singha.
- Hey, Singha.

321
00:29:26,020 --> 00:29:27,370
- Singha. Singha.
- Singha. Singha.

322
00:29:27,910 --> 00:29:29,440
Easy, Singha.

323
00:29:32,150 --> 00:29:33,200
What's wrong with Singha?

324
00:29:34,100 --> 00:29:36,830
Singha. Can you hear me? Singha.

325
00:29:37,930 --> 00:29:39,490
- Singha.
- I don't know what's wrong with him, Mom.

326
00:29:40,240 --> 00:29:42,640
He’s burning up. Should we head to the hospital?

327
00:29:50,150 --> 00:29:53,110
Foon, Joe! Carry Singha to the car. Quick!

328
00:29:53,150 --> 00:29:53,940
- Okay.
- Hurry up!

329
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:57,940
- Count with me.
- Coming! Hold on, hold on!

330
00:29:58,520 --> 00:30:02,080
One, two, three... Up! Got him. He’s in. Okay.

331
00:30:02,180 --> 00:30:04,640
- Oh. Damn it.
- One, two, three.

332
00:30:05,330 --> 00:30:05,900
Oh.

333
00:30:06,560 --> 00:30:08,560
- Careful! Go, go. Watch his head!
- Left, left!

334
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,680
- Left. Left.
- Watch his head! Careful.

335
00:30:09,940 --> 00:30:12,400
- Hurry up, you guys! Be careful!
- Auntie.

336
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,120
Quick! Before it's too late!

337
00:30:16,050 --> 00:30:18,000
- Just grabbed Buddha amulets and ignoring your son!
- Get him in the car.

338
00:30:18,080 --> 00:30:19,120
Ugh, Watch his head.

339
00:30:19,360 --> 00:30:21,230
- Singha,
- Singha, come here.

340
00:30:21,360 --> 00:30:24,320
Hang in there, damn it! Where's all your strength gone?

341
00:30:25,430 --> 00:30:26,380
Fuck!

342
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:32,040
Damn it.

343
00:30:32,760 --> 00:30:35,110
Carrying a fridge for
a friend wasn't even this heavy!

344
00:30:35,590 --> 00:30:38,700
This pair is really looking for trouble lately.

345
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,720
No idea where they're off to this time.

346
00:30:44,060 --> 00:30:46,540
Stay out of it. Worry about yourself.

347
00:30:56,820 --> 00:30:58,930
Guys come help me, quick!

348
00:30:59,050 --> 00:30:59,920
- Quick!
- Yes.

349
00:31:00,400 --> 00:31:01,760
Which way? This way, right?

350
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:02,500
Come.

351
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:04,590
Come. Hurry!

352
00:31:05,180 --> 00:31:06,040
Stay strong, brother.

353
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:07,940
Stay strong, brother.

354
00:31:08,430 --> 00:31:10,660
- Come this way. This way, hurry!
- Strong? He's way past being strong.

355
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,270
- Quickly. Quick!
- Stay strong, brother.

356
00:31:12,510 --> 00:31:13,780
- Stay strong, brother.
- Come. Quickly!

357
00:31:13,820 --> 00:31:15,600
- Watch the stairs!
- Hey! Watch his legs!

358
00:31:15,770 --> 00:31:17,280
My respects, Luang Ta.

359
00:31:17,800 --> 00:31:19,800
You two, hurry up and get Singha inside.

360
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:20,640
Yes, Luang Ta.

361
00:31:22,600 --> 00:31:24,330
Singha is going to be okay, isn't he?

362
00:31:24,360 --> 00:31:25,590
Go inside first.

363
00:31:26,300 --> 00:31:26,840
Yes.

364
00:31:37,080 --> 00:31:38,090
As for you.

365
00:31:38,940 --> 00:31:40,680
Go back to where you belong.

366
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:49,820
Don't create more karma here.

367
00:31:51,060 --> 00:31:51,640
Go.

368
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:08,080
The wandering curse of the wind.

369
00:32:08,850 --> 00:32:10,720
Khmer black magic, carried by the breeze.

370
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:14,410
Your son, Singh, was born on 9th September.

371
00:32:15,080 --> 00:32:20,150
His father intended to pass down
this dark art through his very bloodline.

372
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:23,810
But the dark elements
within him overwhelmed the light.

373
00:32:24,600 --> 00:32:27,240
Your husband fell deep
into the abyss of black magic.

374
00:32:27,830 --> 00:32:29,300
Until he was trapped, with no way out.

375
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:32,840
Let him lie in the enchanted herb bath for now.

376
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:35,220
I will try my own way.

377
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:37,460
It’s going to take some time.

378
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:42,320
But there is no guarantee that
Singha will ever be the same person again.

379
00:32:47,320 --> 00:32:48,430
Sometimes

380
00:32:49,170 --> 00:32:51,840
We can't dictate our own destiny.

381
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:55,090
Only Karma is the one that decides.

382
00:33:04,520 --> 00:33:06,460
(Praying)

383
00:33:06,750 --> 00:33:08,440
(Praying)

384
00:33:08,800 --> 00:33:11,040
(Praying)

385
00:33:11,530 --> 00:33:13,810
(Praying)

386
00:33:13,840 --> 00:33:16,630
(Praying)

387
00:33:26,840 --> 00:33:28,320
Good, good. That's good.

388
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:29,560
Hello, Big Boss.

389
00:33:31,970 --> 00:33:34,320
I'm Arnon.
Is there anything I can do for you, sir?

390
00:33:34,980 --> 00:33:35,840
Sia Rambo.

391
00:33:37,500 --> 00:33:39,920
I’ve heard your name,
but this is the first time we've met in person.

392
00:33:40,420 --> 00:33:41,320
Respect, sir.

393
00:33:41,830 --> 00:33:47,480
Respect? Hell no. People are
dying left and right. What's going on?

394
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:51,100
Are you involved in every single one of these deaths?

395
00:33:52,110 --> 00:33:55,160
And this city. What exactly are you protecting here?

396
00:33:56,010 --> 00:33:56,900
Tell me about it.

397
00:33:59,090 --> 00:34:02,230
I don't know, I'm not involved, and...

398
00:34:02,970 --> 00:34:03,680
Nothing.

399
00:34:06,480 --> 00:34:09,290
- Come on, take a seat first.
- It's alright. I'm just here for business.

400
00:34:09,790 --> 00:34:10,360
It's alright.

401
00:34:10,620 --> 00:34:13,470
Being the provincial governor
doesn't mean you can just do whatever you want.

402
00:34:13,630 --> 00:34:17,540
In this town, you know
there are many layers of powerful people.

403
00:34:17,640 --> 00:34:19,140
You're trash.

404
00:34:19,160 --> 00:34:25,360
I thought my brother, Akkapol
would run this city forever, but now he’s gone.

405
00:34:25,860 --> 00:34:27,490
If that’s all, I’ll be taking my leave now.

406
00:34:29,590 --> 00:34:33,260
Wait! You now I have a huge family.

407
00:34:33,340 --> 00:34:38,910
I can't look after everyone.
Look at this my drug shipment just got ripped off.

408
00:34:39,220 --> 00:34:43,790
My own nephew, Chon, tipped off
the Narcotics Board to bust me and my stash.

409
00:34:44,420 --> 00:34:47,320
And you. You're working
for Senator Namchai, aren't you?

410
00:34:47,550 --> 00:34:49,030
You think I don't know?

411
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:50,420
You piece of shit!

412
00:34:50,930 --> 00:34:53,100
You think you can take over this city? You an idiot!

413
00:34:53,520 --> 00:34:54,610
Get out!

414
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:11,640
(Take care of it.)

415
00:35:20,720 --> 00:35:21,520
Chicken.

416
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:33,520
You bastard.

417
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:37,560
Sia! Sia, what's wrong?

418
00:35:38,530 --> 00:35:39,440
Sia.

419
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:42,120
Security! Help!

420
00:35:43,540 --> 00:35:44,360
Fuck.

421
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:02,000
This city is so beautiful at night.

422
00:36:05,610 --> 00:36:07,480
But I suppose it’s worth the effort of...

423
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:10,280
Kneeling and begging for mercy,

424
00:36:11,570 --> 00:36:12,600
Pleading.

425
00:36:17,350 --> 00:36:19,030
Only to betray them in cold blood.

426
00:36:23,900 --> 00:36:24,870
Well...

427
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:26,680
Quite worth it, indeed.

428
00:36:31,880 --> 00:36:32,980
With you by my side,

429
00:36:35,160 --> 00:36:37,840
Everything just seems so easy.

430
00:36:41,990 --> 00:36:43,300
But it costs a fortune.

431
00:36:46,740 --> 00:36:47,380
Okay.

432
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:56,860
The person I’ve been looking for is getting close.

433
00:37:01,840 --> 00:37:03,890
Who? This person you're searching for?

434
00:37:10,240 --> 00:37:11,910
The one I have some unfinished business with.

435
00:37:46,580 --> 00:37:47,440
Bitch!

436
00:37:49,870 --> 00:37:50,980
Where the hell are you going?

437
00:37:54,690 --> 00:37:55,420
What are you doing?

438
00:37:55,980 --> 00:37:56,870
Stay out of this!

439
00:38:09,070 --> 00:38:09,880
You demon!

440
00:38:10,860 --> 00:38:12,010
You think you can take my life?

441
00:38:13,610 --> 00:38:14,880
Never.

442
00:38:17,850 --> 00:38:19,870
You’re not getting my life!

443
00:38:41,750 --> 00:38:43,000
We have three bodies at the scene.

444
00:38:43,690 --> 00:38:45,980
The middle- aged male is a former
Member of Parliament for the Phumtham Party.

445
00:38:46,510 --> 00:38:47,720
His name is Mr. Weerawat Nalodom.

446
00:38:48,710 --> 00:38:50,350
The middle- aged female is identified as his wife.

447
00:38:51,080 --> 00:38:51,990
And the teenage victim.

448
00:38:52,520 --> 00:38:53,290
Is their son.

449
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:06,080
No, that’s not right.

450
00:39:06,670 --> 00:39:07,980
There’s a girl in the bedroom.

451
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:09,840
Inspector.

452
00:39:10,650 --> 00:39:12,840
This doesn't look like a normal incident anymore.

453
00:39:13,370 --> 00:39:17,030
The patterns of death are highly
unusual across the board.

454
00:39:17,940 --> 00:39:20,480
And every victim is tied to politics and bribery.

455
00:39:20,810 --> 00:39:23,180
What kind of city is this?
There are hardly any reporters.

456
00:39:23,700 --> 00:39:25,110
It’s like people die
and then just vanish into thin air.

457
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:27,270
No news, no leads,
no evidence linking anything together.

458
00:39:27,590 --> 00:39:29,130
Witnesses are kept silent by fear.

459
00:39:29,520 --> 00:39:30,480
Talk and end up dead.

460
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,550
What a civilized country we live in.

461
00:39:39,160 --> 00:39:39,600
Lieutenant.

462
00:39:40,780 --> 00:39:41,450
Look at this.

463
00:39:43,680 --> 00:39:47,280
They’ve decoded the security footage.

464
00:39:53,760 --> 00:39:54,680
You bastard.

465
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:56,950
You're coming for my life?

466
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:07,070
And all that.

467
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:10,700
It’s just like every other case we’ve had.

468
00:40:11,560 --> 00:40:13,500
There was no trace of the killer.

469
00:40:15,050 --> 00:40:16,700
No hired gun.

470
00:40:17,650 --> 00:40:20,640
Every case looks like a suicide.

471
00:40:21,020 --> 00:40:22,170
Or just an accident.

472
00:40:24,760 --> 00:40:26,390
It looks like an overdose.

473
00:40:27,460 --> 00:40:28,920
Or a severe mental breakdown.

474
00:40:32,630 --> 00:40:34,300
Or if there’s a real connection here.

475
00:40:35,320 --> 00:40:37,010
It has to be related to this.

476
00:40:38,280 --> 00:40:39,070
The drugs?

477
00:40:40,110 --> 00:40:41,910
And how does that link to homicide cases?

478
00:40:42,610 --> 00:40:44,080
All the evidence in our hands.

479
00:40:44,430 --> 00:40:47,330
Shows a connection to this
specific drug at every crime scene.

480
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:49,310
It must come from the same source.

481
00:40:51,060 --> 00:40:52,960
I’ll do my best to trace it back to the source.

482
00:41:02,300 --> 00:41:04,100
(Praying)

483
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:06,110
(Praying)

484
00:41:26,240 --> 00:41:27,910
Thank you very much, Mr. Arnon.

485
00:41:27,960 --> 00:41:31,240
For providing scholarships
to these underprivileged children.

486
00:41:31,910 --> 00:41:32,740
It’s my pleasure.

487
00:41:33,800 --> 00:41:36,720
Then, I’d like to take a picture for the records.

488
00:41:37,170 --> 00:41:37,950
Yes, sure.

489
00:41:38,360 --> 00:41:39,960
Children, please form a line.

490
00:41:46,200 --> 00:41:48,480
Ohm... thump- thump, thump- thump.

491
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:50,640
Heavy stone, solid within.

492
00:41:51,040 --> 00:41:52,670
My skull is forged in steel

493
00:41:53,170 --> 00:41:57,360
Against diamond blades,
spears, wooden arrows, and firelocks.

494
00:41:57,820 --> 00:42:02,940
By the power of merit, magic,
and the essence of a hundred and eight roots.

495
00:42:03,430 --> 00:42:06,200
Descend and dwell within my body.

496
00:42:06,870 --> 00:42:08,800
(Chanting)

497
00:42:09,120 --> 00:42:10,640
(Chanting)

498
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:12,320
(Chanting)

499
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:14,280
(Chanting)

500
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:16,240
(Chanting)

501
00:42:16,730 --> 00:42:17,760
From now on.

502
00:42:18,200 --> 00:42:20,460
You shall be invulnerable.

503
00:42:20,720 --> 00:42:22,120
No blade can cut you, no bullet can pierce you.

504
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:27,510
Singha, damn it! What's the plan?

505
00:42:28,470 --> 00:42:30,150
They betrayed each other.
They're coming for the drugs.

506
00:42:30,190 --> 00:42:31,840
And they're everywhere outside!

507
00:42:33,050 --> 00:42:33,820
Shit!

508
00:42:34,940 --> 00:42:36,340
Singha, I’m scared.

509
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:40,720
Follow my lead.

510
00:42:44,360 --> 00:42:45,840
- Hey.
- Shit, Singha.

511
00:42:52,430 --> 00:42:53,250
We're fucked!

512
00:42:55,210 --> 00:42:57,310
Those bastards! Goddamn!

513
00:43:05,900 --> 00:43:07,000
Bastards!

514
00:43:27,190 --> 00:43:27,920
Joe.

515
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:29,880
Come on.

516
00:43:43,790 --> 00:43:44,560
Singha.

517
00:43:45,450 --> 00:43:47,090
I'm sure the cops are gonna come after us.

518
00:43:50,360 --> 00:43:51,820
Just act normal, Joe.

519
00:43:56,520 --> 00:44:00,570
I’m telling you, those dealers
are definitely gonna come and kill us.

520
00:44:01,170 --> 00:44:02,180
And then there’s home.

521
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:05,380
The cops might not know, but I bet they do.

522
00:44:05,970 --> 00:44:07,520
They’re definitely coming to finish us off.

523
00:44:13,110 --> 00:44:14,560
Go home now and don't make a sound.

524
00:44:16,240 --> 00:44:17,760
- Go.
- How about you?

525
00:44:18,560 --> 00:44:20,800
Leave! I told you to leave! Go!

526
00:44:34,400 --> 00:44:35,640
Woah, chill the fuck out, man!

527
00:44:35,750 --> 00:44:36,820
Why you jonesing so hard?

528
00:44:39,990 --> 00:44:40,560
Give me the money.

529
00:44:43,340 --> 00:44:44,120
I'll call you.

530
00:44:44,440 --> 00:44:45,590
- Hey, what are you up to?
- Hey!

531
00:44:45,680 --> 00:44:47,640
Hey, what are you doing?

532
00:44:51,470 --> 00:44:52,420
Selling drugs.

533
00:44:55,030 --> 00:44:57,350
You’re dealing drugs right outside the precinct?

534
00:44:58,990 --> 00:44:59,560
Go.

535
00:45:01,240 --> 00:45:02,120
Hey, I told you to go! Just walk!

536
00:45:02,540 --> 00:45:03,010
Go.

537
00:45:07,740 --> 00:45:09,000
Singha's been busted, man.

538
00:45:09,770 --> 00:45:10,730
What's Next?

539
00:45:18,080 --> 00:45:19,110
Have you eaten yet?

540
00:45:20,600 --> 00:45:21,430
Yes, I have.

541
00:45:24,440 --> 00:45:25,640
You'll be out soon.

542
00:45:28,590 --> 00:45:30,440
I left some things for you with the guard.

543
00:45:30,970 --> 00:45:34,360
Luckily, business is slow
because of the long weekend.

544
00:45:34,830 --> 00:45:37,370
I made a big bag of Kaphrao
with bamboo shoots for you.

545
00:45:38,120 --> 00:45:40,110
Share it with the other guys inside, okay?

546
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:44,260
Mom.

547
00:45:46,110 --> 00:45:48,100
I'm sorry.

548
00:45:48,550 --> 00:45:49,050
Mom.

549
00:45:50,200 --> 00:45:52,100
- Mom.
- I’m heading out now, Officer.

550
00:45:52,510 --> 00:45:55,090
I brought some snacks for you as well, Officer.

551
00:45:57,410 --> 00:45:59,010
Please take care of my son.

552
00:46:22,860 --> 00:46:24,070
It’s karma.

553
00:46:26,120 --> 00:46:27,600
It depends on how he uses that karma.

554
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:29,480
Whether for good or for evil.

555
00:46:31,400 --> 00:46:33,250
His destiny is quite more special than others.

556
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:36,950
It's unlikely to be karma
trailing him from a past life.

557
00:46:38,080 --> 00:46:39,840
It’s bound to these dens of vice.

558
00:46:43,520 --> 00:46:45,840
I don't want him to end up like his father.

559
00:46:48,700 --> 00:46:50,500
Who can escape their fate?

560
00:46:52,880 --> 00:46:53,840
Just look at me.

561
00:46:54,760 --> 00:46:56,490
I should never have gotten into this life.

562
00:46:57,130 --> 00:46:59,600
It haunts you, forced to live in the shadows.

563
00:47:00,840 --> 00:47:02,200
(Praying)

564
00:47:02,540 --> 00:47:04,480
(Praying)

565
00:47:12,240 --> 00:47:12,690
Singha.

566
00:47:14,300 --> 00:47:15,090
Singha, Son.

567
00:47:16,310 --> 00:47:16,930
Singha.

568
00:47:18,960 --> 00:47:19,600
Singha.

569
00:47:20,690 --> 00:47:21,920
Can you hear me? Singha.

570
00:47:22,810 --> 00:47:23,600
Singha, Son.

571
00:47:29,960 --> 00:47:31,830
What happened? What's wrong with me?

572
00:47:34,390 --> 00:47:34,980
Singha.

573
00:47:38,430 --> 00:47:40,560
After tonight, you'll never be the same again.

574
00:47:42,010 --> 00:47:43,400
Your fate has reached its end.

575
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:46,800
Someone is looking to take your soul for a ritual.

576
00:47:48,100 --> 00:47:49,010
A man without a soul.

577
00:47:49,530 --> 00:47:51,030
You know what that means?

578
00:47:53,140 --> 00:47:54,040
Are you insane?

579
00:47:55,260 --> 00:47:56,390
What are you talking about?

580
00:47:56,810 --> 00:47:58,220
I don't understand.

581
00:47:59,420 --> 00:48:00,650
I'll tell you about it later.

582
00:48:02,280 --> 00:48:05,140
They’re starting to find out that I’m back.

583
00:48:10,610 --> 00:48:11,810
About what I saw that day.

584
00:48:13,160 --> 00:48:14,250
When they shot you.

585
00:48:15,770 --> 00:48:16,640
What was that?

586
00:48:19,190 --> 00:48:20,300
Were you wearing a vest?

587
00:48:23,110 --> 00:48:24,440
Or are you actually bulletproof?

588
00:48:26,230 --> 00:48:27,620
You have to learn that for yourself, Singha.

589
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:29,590
I need to get moving.

590
00:48:31,140 --> 00:48:32,860
If I stay any longer, they'll definitely find me.

591
00:48:39,200 --> 00:48:40,120
Mom.

592
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:42,700
Singha.

593
00:48:52,510 --> 00:48:53,060
Mom.

594
00:48:55,840 --> 00:48:58,120
There’s so much you haven't told me, Mom.

595
00:49:34,810 --> 00:49:37,230
Another one of those sorcerers has arrived?
